@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-s46a-overall-ceiling`
IMPORT `ito-s46b-advance-base`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for ss 46A and 46B. Row IL-27. Expected values worked by hand from lines 1754 and 1757 before the rules were run; none edited.
-- s 46A: credit sums + R&D deduction <= 50% of taxable income before the R&D deduction. Taxable income 200,000: ceiling 100,000.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — sections 46A and 46B`

GIVEN `credit`    IS A NUMBER
      `deduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Donations and research and development in a tax year, for section 46A`
`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` `credit` `and a deduction of` `deduction` MEANS
    `Donations and research and development in a tax year, for section 46A` OF 2026, 200000, `credit`, `deduction`

§§ `Section 46A — under or at the ceiling`

-- 60,000 + 30,000 = 90,000 <= 100,000: both unchanged. 70,000 + 30,000 = 100,000, exactly at the ceiling: unchanged.
#ASSERT `the sums on which the credit under section 46 is given after section 46A for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 60000 `and a deduction of` 30000) EQUALS 60000
#ASSERT `the sums deducted for research and development after section 46A for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 60000 `and a deduction of` 30000) EQUALS 30000
#ASSERT `the sums on which the credit under section 46 is given after section 46A for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 70000 `and a deduction of` 30000) EQUALS 70000
#ASSERT `the sums deducted for research and development after section 46A for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 70000 `and a deduction of` 30000) EQUALS 30000
-- Nothing of either: nothing.
#ASSERT `the sums on which the credit under section 46 is given after section 46A for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 0 `and a deduction of` 0) EQUALS 0

§§ `Section 46A — over the ceiling (fork F8)`

-- 60,000 + 50,000 = 110,000 > 100,000. The credit cut first: credit = 100,000 - 50,000 = 50,000, deduction 50,000.
-- The deduction cut first: credit stays 60,000, deduction = 100,000 - 60,000 = 40,000. The default declines.
#ASSERT `the sums on which the credit under section 46 is given after section 46A, reading the cut as` `the credit is cut first` `, for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 60000 `and a deduction of` 50000) EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `the sums deducted for research and development after section 46A, reading the cut as` `the credit is cut first` `, for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 60000 `and a deduction of` 50000) EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `the sums on which the credit under section 46 is given after section 46A, reading the cut as` `the deduction is cut first` `, for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 60000 `and a deduction of` 50000) EQUALS 60000
#ASSERT `the sums deducted for research and development after section 46A, reading the cut as` `the deduction is cut first` `, for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 60000 `and a deduction of` 50000) EQUALS 40000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the sums on which the credit under section 46 is given after section 46A for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 60000 `and a deduction of` 50000) BECAUSE "section 46A does not say whether the credit or the deduction is cut first, and here the total passes the ceiling"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the sums deducted for research and development after section 46A for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 60000 `and a deduction of` 50000) BECAUSE "section 46A does not say whether the credit or the deduction is cut first, and here the total passes the ceiling"
-- A deduction alone above the ceiling (120,000) with credit sums of 10,000: the credit cut first leaves no room (0) and the deduction is held to 100,000;
-- the deduction cut first keeps the 10,000 and the deduction is 90,000.
#ASSERT `the sums on which the credit under section 46 is given after section 46A, reading the cut as` `the credit is cut first` `, for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 10000 `and a deduction of` 120000) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the sums deducted for research and development after section 46A, reading the cut as` `the credit is cut first` `, for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 10000 `and a deduction of` 120000) EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `the sums on which the credit under section 46 is given after section 46A, reading the cut as` `the deduction is cut first` `, for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 10000 `and a deduction of` 120000) EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the sums deducted for research and development after section 46A, reading the cut as` `the deduction is cut first` `, for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 10000 `and a deduction of` 120000) EQUALS 90000
-- A credit alone above the ceiling (130,000), no deduction: both cuts hold it to 100,000, but the default still declines (it asks only whether the total passes).
#ASSERT `the sums on which the credit under section 46 is given after section 46A, reading the cut as` `the credit is cut first` `, for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 130000 `and a deduction of` 0) EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `the sums on which the credit under section 46 is given after section 46A, reading the cut as` `the deduction is cut first` `, for` (`with taxable income 200,000 in 2026, credit sums` 130000 `and a deduction of` 0) EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `section 46A — the reading row IL-27 takes of the cut` EQUALS `declined where the total passes the ceiling`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the sums on which the credit under section 46 is given after section 46A for` (`Donations and research and development in a tax year, for section 46A` OF 2023, 200000, 1000, 0) BECAUSE "row IL-27 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"

§§ `Section 46B — the base for advance payments`

-- A base of 10,000 and 3,500 of tax relieved by the donations credit: 13,500. No relief: unchanged. Before 2024: refused.
#ASSERT `the base for advance payments after section 46B in tax year` 2026 `, the base before the addition being` 10000 `and the tax relieved by credit for donations` 3500 EQUALS 13500
#ASSERT `the base for advance payments after section 46B in tax year` 2026 `, the base before the addition being` 10000 `and the tax relieved by credit for donations` 0 EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the base for advance payments after section 46B in tax year` 2024 `, the base before the addition being` 0 `and the tax relieved by credit for donations` 3500 EQUALS 3500
#ASSERT REFUSED `the base for advance payments after section 46B in tax year` 2023 `, the base before the addition being` 10000 `and the tax relieved by credit for donations` 3500 BECAUSE "row IL-27 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"
